  "protocol": "Bankroll Network",
  "name": "Bankroll Stack drip pays a same-transaction buyer for the whole idle period",
  "summary": "The BankrollNetworkStack template's distribute() credits stakers 2% of dividendBalance_ per day for all the time since lastPayout, without capping it at the pool, and buy() mints the buyer's stake before calling it. The Ethereum StackPlus LINK pool had been idle for 289 days, so the attacker flash-bought a dominant stake, which the first distribution credited 5.8 times the drip pool, then sold and withdrew; buyFor() pulls from six wallets with standing LINK approvals supplied the LINK paid out.",
