  "notes": [
    "One defect in one template: the campaign hit Bankroll's own Stack deployments on Ethereum and BSC and verbatim forks with the same distribute() and buy order (DrippingFinance, Sinstake, ABS, StakingNetwork, QRT and VIVA pools on BSC, WSPP on Polygon). The Gangsterfinance TokenVault, rewritten code exploited separately, and the 2024 Bankroll buyFor-beneficiary record are other incidents.",
    "The anchor also used buyFor(), which pulls from any approving address, to move 818.9 LINK from six wallets into the pool before withdrawing; their LINK left them and counts as victim depletion, as do the six forced buys in 0x5382925a.",
    "Campaign: every transaction on Ethereum, BSC, Polygon, Avalanche, Arbitrum and Base whose logs show onTokenPurchase, onTokenSell and onWithdraw for one customer on one contract, with a net outflow from it; none precedes the anchor except the 2024 buyFor exploits. Left out: owner pause/reinvest cycle 0x3628d51c and six zero-outflow 0x313e71df transactions.",
    "Drip, ZOMBIE, ABS, SIN, QRT, VIVA and WSPP have no price and are valued at the BNB or POL the attackers got for them; the FluffyCorgi was never sold."
  ]
